set -euo pipefail

# Disabled 2026-08-28: this hook used to force-mirror every `git push
# origin` (blocking any other remote name) to two Cambridge corporate
# repos and self-heal remote.origin.pushurl back to those two URLs,
# silently excluding the actual GitHub origin (CarlDog/certmate.git)
# from push targets. It went from committed-but-inert to actively
# enforcing the moment core.hooksPath got wired to .githooks/ for
# unrelated gitleaks/PII work, and pushed this repo's full commit
# history (not a subtree-filtered slice) as a new branch onto:
#   - https://github.com/CarlDog-Cambridge/InventoryManagement.git
#     (redirects server-side to Cambridge.ProdSpt.IRIS)
#   - https://dev.azure.com/Cambridge-Technology/ProductionSupport/_git/InventoryManagement
# Both were cleaned up (branch deleted) the same day. See CLAUDE memory
# certmate-security-risk.md for the full incident writeup.
#
# If a real, deliberate mirror to the Cambridge InventoryManagement/IRIS
# repo is wanted later, it should be a `git subtree push` (or equivalent)
# scoped to .inventorymanagement/ only, run explicitly — not a blanket
# full-history mirror silently triggered by every `git push origin`.
exit 0
